# Evaluation image assets are DOWNLOADED, never committed.
#
# Every case in manifest.json records a public source page and a public asset
# URL instead of the bytes. `fetch_assets.py` resolves those URLs into this
# directory on demand. Nothing here is tracked: the repository must never carry
# an image payload, and the licences involved are honoured by pointing at the
# original file page rather than redistributing a copy from here.
assets/

# Evaluation results are GENERATED, never committed.
#
# A results file records what one run observed: labels, identifiers, provider
# modes, counts and sanitized error class names. It is safe by construction, but
# it is still generated output, it is large, and a committed copy would rot the
# moment the benchmark or the agent moved. Phase 3 attaches the results it wants
# to preserve to its own report instead.
results/
